# What ships is an allowlist, not a list of exclusions.
#
# The payload is 453 files. While this file ignored /css/, /js/, /img/, /media/,
# /data/, /svg/ and /fonts/, `git status` reported a clean tree with 449 of them
# untracked-and-invisible, and `git add -A` on launch day would have published an
# index.html pointing at files that were not in the commit: no stylesheet, no
# scripts, no video, no images, and nothing failing loudly enough to notice.
#
# So: ignore everything, then allow exactly the directories the page loads from.
# `git status` now shows the real payload, and `python3 build/publish_check.py`
# compares the tracked set against what is on disk before the push.
#
# site/svg/ is deliberately NOT here. The seven charts are inlined into
# index.html by build/build_site.py; the .svg and .table.html files under svg/
# are the build's own inputs, nothing on the page links them, and shipping them
# would put a second, silently drifting copy of every chart on the web.

/*
!/.gitignore
!/.nojekyll
!/index.html
!/results.html
!/trials.html
!/watch.html
!/agent-as-policy.pdf
!/robots.txt
!/css/
!/js/
!/fonts/
!/img/
!/media/
!/data/

# never, anywhere under the allowed directories
.DS_Store
*.tmp
Thumbs.db
